<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">born 1961</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mohamed bin Zayed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-nahyan">Al Nahyan</a> is the ruler of Abu Dhabi and has been president of the United Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirates</a> since May 2022. A son of the founding president <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zayed-bin-sultan-al-nahyan">Zayed bin Sultan Al Nahyan</a>, he became crown prince of Abu Dhabi in 2004 and was the country's de facto leader during the illness of his half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalifa">Khalifa</a>, building up its armed forces and an assertive regional foreign policy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mohamed-bin-zayed-al-nahyan.jpg" alt="Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Press Service of the President of the Republic of Azerbaijan · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mohamed_bin_Zayed_Al_Nahyan_-_2024_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
